.TP
.B w
Default view: every logged-in user, full column set.
.TP
.B w \-s
Short view: \fIUSER\fR \fITTY\fR \fIIDLE\fR \fIWHAT\fR only. Useful
on narrow terminals.
.TP
.B w alice
Show only sessions belonging to user \fIalice\fR.
.TP
.B w \-f
Add the \fIFROM\fR column to see where each session was opened from
(SSH host, display, or local seat).
.TP
.B w \-fi
Same as \fB\-f\fR but show IP addresses instead of resolved
hostnames in the \fIFROM\fR column. Faster on hosts where reverse
DNS is slow.
.TP
.B w \-p
Show the login PID and the foreground PID side by side in the
\fIWHAT\fR column, in the form \fIloginpid\fR\fB/\fR\fIwhatpid\fR.
.TP
.B w \-h | wc \-l
Count active sessions without the header noise.
.TP
.B w \-o
Old-style output: idle times below one minute show as a blank cell.
Useful when sub-minute precision is just visual clutter.
